I think a useful addition to the game would be some indication of the
direction from which you are being attacked by something which you can't see.
This would apply to invisible monsters, and to all monsters when the player
is blinded and non-telepathic.

For example, 

	It hits! (north) It bites! (northwest) -- more --

would seem more realistic.  You may even throw in a small chance of having
the direction incorrectly given (off by one square -- the biting monster might
actually be west, rather than northwest....)

If something bites me in real life, I would have some indication of what part
of me is being attacked, and could at least determine the direction from which
the teeth are coming.

After all, when you're invisible and attack a monster, it knows where you are
and attacks back....  (Assuming you're not using throwing weapons.)

